/-!
# Atlas V-03 (block C): linearised Maxwell combinations around Kerr–Newman (sources of `res1d`, `res1dN`)

V-02's `np_maxwell_combo` (`np_maxwell_combo_neg`) holds for every null frame and every antisymmetric `C^∞` field, with
the right-hand sides of the NP Maxwell equations (sources `J`, `H`, `Φ₀`, `Φ₂` kept) written as
`mxS1, mxS2` (`mxS4, mxS3` for the negative branch; class-B notation for V-02's inline expressions). At KN these
source combinations vanish on the open slice (`certReg`: `J = 0`, `dF = 0`; `Φ₀ = Φ₂ = κ = σ = λ = ν = 0`), so the
frame-variation terms of their frame derivatives vanish (proved), and their first variations are the explicit
`srcS1 … srcS4` (Maxwell residual variations `HfrVar`, `JfrVar` and the `Φ₀` / `Φ₂` variation `FfrFVar`, kept). -/

open Complex Filter Topology
open scoped ComplexConjugate Matrix ContDiff
open ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell ExactVacuumAtlas.Variation
open ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.KN (Sig Del gKN giKN domReg domKN faradayKN)

